<p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if your business trades cross-border into or out of Italy, don''t treat "ViDA compliance" and "Italian SdI compliance" as two separate future projects to plan for separately. Given how closely the derogation''s expiry lines up with ViDA''s own cross-border timeline, the more useful planning assumption is that whatever you build for Italy today likely forms a meaningful part of what you''ll need for EU-wide cross-border reporting later, rather than a system you''ll need to replace wholesale.</p>');
